@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-utility-functions Utility functions
@brief Utility functions for handling strings in tests.

@details
The `utility` namespace has three functions for the strings that the
tests often check:
- `utility::is_match (input, pattern)` checks whether a string matches a
  pattern, in which `*` matches any sequence of characters, including an
  empty one, and `?` matches any single character;
- `utility::split (input, delimiters)` splits a string into a vector of
  the non-empty sub-strings separated by any of the delimiter characters;
  for a `std::string` it returns `std::string` copies, and for a
  `std::string_view`, a string literal, or a `const char*` it returns
  views into the input, which must outlive them;
- `utility::extract_file_name (path)` returns the file name part of a
  path, after the last `/` or backslash.

@par Example

@code{.cpp}
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

ts.test ("Check the strings", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::utility::is_match ("main.cpp", "*.cpp"));
  t.expect (mt::eq (mt::utility::split ("a, b,,c", ", ").size (), 3u));
  t.expect (mt::eq (mt::utility::extract_file_name ("src/main.cpp"),
                    "main.cpp"));
});
@endcode
